        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\u0022risks\u0022:[{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that supply stays short of demand and holds back how fast orders turn into revenue\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest quarter revenue\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u0022$1.93 billion\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management called supply the governor of near-term revenue and said demand is not the limiter, so revenue below the low end of its own outlook range would show supply capping conversion\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that profitability slips because a one-time tariff benefit does not repeat\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022fact\u0022:\u0022latest quarter gross margin\u0022},\u0022direction\u0022:\u0022falls below\u0022,\u0022level\u0022:\u002265.87%\u0022,\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the chief financial officer said one-time tariff impacts this year artificially lifted profitability and will not repeat, so a lower gross margin would show that lift fading\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that export controls, tariffs or trade policy restrict sales or raise costs\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:1,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022a new export control rule or tariff measure is announced that limits Keysight\u0027s sales or raises its costs\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022regulatory\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022the results release lists export control regulations and compliance and tariff and trade policy among the uncertainties that could make results differ materially from management\u0027s expectations, so a new measure would show the risk arriving\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:1},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that savings from the recent acquisitions fall short of what management expects\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022management lowers its expectation for realised cost synergies from the recent acquisitions or reports new integration problems\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022acquisition\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management said integration is largely complete and expects most of its synergy target to be realised on a run rate basis by the end of the fiscal year, so any cut to that expectation would show the savings falling short\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3},{\u0022risk\u0022:\u0022that AI infrastructure spending slows and removes the main driver of growth\u0022,\u0022riskDocument\u0022:3,\u0022confirm\u0022:{\u0022event\u0022:\u0022hyperscalers or other AI data centre builders cut spending and Keysight\u0027s wireline orders fall\u0022,\u0022kind\u0022:\u0022other\u0022},\u0022why\u0022:\u0022management attributed record wireline orders and the first quarter in which wireline revenue exceeded wireless to the rapid scaling of the AI infrastructure ecosystem, so a spending cut would hit the largest growth driver\u0022,\u0022whyDocument\u0022:3}]}"
